- If there exist two distinct indices `i` and `j` in the integer array parameter `nums` such that the elements at those indices are equal and the absolute difference between `i` and `j` is less than or equal to the integer parameter `k`, the boolean result is equal to the true literal.
- If there does not exist two distinct indices `i` and `j` in the integer array parameter `nums` such that the elements at those indices are equal and the absolute difference between `i` and `j` is less than or equal to the integer parameter `k`, the boolean result is equal to the false literal.
- The length of the integer array parameter `nums` is less than or equal to 100000.
- All values in the integer array parameter `nums` are greater than or equal to -1000000000 and are less than or equal to 1000000000.
- The integer parameter `k` is less than or equal to 100000.